	spec: "The model picker is the old Hal's tree (tasks/w4/forms.md, Model picker): provider, family or vendor, models; ▶/▼ show closed and open categories, right/left open and close them, Enter on a category picks its default (gpt → gpt-6-sol, opus → opus 5.5). A provider's families go most capable first (fable, opus, sonnet, haiku, then by name); in a family, newest version first and same-version variants plain, sol, terra, luna, then by name. A family lists its two newest versions' flagship variants (plain, sol, terra, luna, astra: gpt 6 and 5.6, opus 5.5 and 5); its older versions and other variants (mini, pro, codex, daybreak…) wait in a closed family/older category. A direct provider with families puts non-chat models (image, realtime, audio, tts, transcribe, embedding, moderation, search…) and family-less ones (o3) in a closed provider/other. These buckets come last in their category and have no default, so Enter opens them. A dated snapshot (-20251101) hides behind its undated alias; the current model always shows, its categories open. Rows use the models.dev name as is. Typing matches categories too and selects the matching one first (gp → openai/gpt, opus → anthropic/opus), else the best-scoring model; ties go to an alias's model (claude → Opus 5.5), else to the higher row. Left and right open and close categories even while searching (the search box keeps its text; Ctrl-A/E move in it); typing reopens every matching category. Modal text fields have Ctrl-A/E, Ctrl-U/K and Alt-Backspace (Ctrl-W stays close-tab). Modals are 80% of the rows, at most 36.",
